{"changes":["cmd/capture.go: added dimensionForToken, the token-to-Knowledge-Dimension table taken from the standard's token overview (vis/str=intent, req=requirements, fnd=research, arc=architecture, adr/dec=decisions, spec=specifications, std=standards, gls=vocabulary, scp/epc/plan/trc=planning, rvw=quality, run=operations, rel/shr=records; operating tokens deliberately return none). The value is now set on both NewDraft calls, which is what R6 requires.","cmd/capture.go: added excludeTransportPaths/captureTransportDirs mirroring the code-graph skip-list (exchange, .eka, drafts, feedback, plus .ekapkg archives), applied to the merged file list before classification. Snapshot filenames like exchange/snapshots/.../dec-foo-v1/unit.json can no longer decide the artifact type of a source change.","cmd/capture.go: added classifyPathSignals so family signals are read from whole path segments and basenames instead of substring matching the joined file list.","cmd/capture.go: replaced the contradictory confidence branch (confidence = threshold - 0.05, still below the threshold it was meant to satisfy, then clamped to 0.4) with captureConfidenceFloor and isSpeculativeToken. The threshold now gates only the speculative token (sto chosen from a word in commit prose); a token backed by an explicit path segment is evidence and is never downgraded."],"role":"implementation","summary":"Fixed the capture gateway so reconciled drafts carry a valid dimension, ignore transport paths, and no longer downgrade path-backed evidence by a confidence threshold.","tests":["Unit: cmd/capture_classify_test.go - transport paths excluded; source-only change not classified as a knowledge artifact; every knowledge token maps to its standard dimension while every operating token maps to none; confidence never falls below the floor; path evidence (specification/, adr/, plans/) not downgraded by the threshold.","End-to-end before/after with a synthetic repo: a commit touching specification/overview.md previously produced spec-add-specification-overview with dimension missing -\u003e R6 error, 'Verdict: FAIL'. After the fix it produces dimension 'specifications' -\u003e 'valid (0 errors)', and eka publish succeeded (would previously have been impossible).","A change confined to cmd/*.go now yields bug- or ch- and never spec-/adr-/plan- from snapshot filenames.","go build ./... , go vet ./cmd/, gofmt clean."]}